sentences.l:
and there dwelt
Aeolus, Hippotes’ son, dear to the immortal gods,
on a floating island;

Nine days alike we sailed, both nights and day,
and on the tenth already was appearing the fatherland’s soil,
and now men tending fires we were seeing, being near;

then me indeed sweet sleep came upon, worn out,
for always the foot of the ship I was handling, and to no other
of my companions had I given it, that more quickly we might reach our fatherland;

Many from Troy he is carrying off, fair treasures
of the booty, but we in turn, the same road having completed,
homeward are going, empty hands along with us having;

But when of food and of drink we had partaken,
then indeed I, a herald having taken with me and a companion,
went to the famous halls of Aeolus;
